1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,760
Some documents are too
big to click together.

2
00:00:02,837 --> 00:00:08,634
The 2026 planner has 365 day pages,
and nobody made those one at a time:

3
00:00:08,634 --> 00:00:10,977
a short script built them.

4
00:00:11,109 --> 00:00:15,249
This episode is about the generator,
and writing a script of your own.

5
00:00:15,460 --> 00:00:19,340
The purple Generator button
opens two editors side by side.

6
00:00:19,488 --> 00:00:22,534
The left script returns
templates, the designs.

7
00:00:22,640 --> 00:00:27,840
The right one returns pages: the hierarchy,
with each page naming its template.

8
00:00:28,050 --> 00:00:30,330
I'll paste in a script for the templates.

9
00:00:30,380 --> 00:00:34,305
Two A4 templates: a week page,
with a grid listing its days,

10
00:00:34,305 --> 00:00:37,903
and a day page, with the date,
a link back to the week,

11
00:00:37,903 --> 00:00:39,200
and lined paper.

12
00:00:39,337 --> 00:00:43,017
They are the same elements you
draw by hand, written as data.

13
00:00:43,225 --> 00:00:44,995
And a hierarchy script.

14
00:00:45,060 --> 00:00:48,604
A top page for the week, then
a loop that makes seven days,

15
00:00:48,604 --> 00:00:51,488
each with a title, a
template, and a date field,

16
00:00:51,488 --> 00:00:54,020
worked out from the start of the week.

17
00:00:54,228 --> 00:00:59,405
Preview runs both scripts in a sealed
sandbox, with no network and a ten second

18
00:00:59,405 --> 00:01:00,048
limit.

19
00:01:00,139 --> 00:01:02,019
Your project is not touched.

20
00:01:02,225 --> 00:01:07,191
The preview has one card per template,
each drawn with real generated data:

21
00:01:07,191 --> 00:01:08,765
the week, and a day.

22
00:01:08,819 --> 00:01:12,928
A card marked Unused would mean
no page asked for that template,

23
00:01:12,928 --> 00:01:14,719
which is usually a typo.

24
00:01:14,927 --> 00:01:18,476
Create As New Project opens
the result in its own tab,

25
00:01:18,476 --> 00:01:20,697
and leaves this project alone.

26
00:01:20,731 --> 00:01:25,671
Replace Current Project swaps it in
here instead, as one step you can undo.

27
00:01:25,880 --> 00:01:30,470
Here it is, in a new tab: eight pages
from about thirty lines of code.

28
00:01:30,619 --> 00:01:34,669
The week page lists its days,
and each day page has its date.

29
00:01:34,879 --> 00:01:37,099
The scripts are saved with the project.

30
00:01:37,153 --> 00:01:41,883
Open the generator again, and the preset
menu offers Current saved source.

31
00:01:42,021 --> 00:01:43,911
Opening it never runs it.

32
00:01:43,977 --> 00:01:46,497
Nothing runs until you press Preview.

33
00:01:46,704 --> 00:01:51,168
From here, the canvas works as
usual: let code build the structure,

34
00:01:51,168 --> 00:01:53,484
then polish the design by hand.

35
00:01:53,586 --> 00:01:58,546
Just remember that running the scripts again
with Replace starts over from the code.

36
00:01:58,758 --> 00:02:00,138
Let's export it.

37
00:02:00,217 --> 00:02:03,917
The week page lists all seven
days, and each one is a link.

38
00:02:04,037 --> 00:02:08,766
Every date came from the script, so planning
another week is a matter of changing

39
00:02:08,766 --> 00:02:10,767
one date and running it again.

40
00:02:10,980 --> 00:02:15,520
Next time, we leave the editor: the
gallery, accounts, and saving to the cloud.
